# Overnight batch logs: 241MB of verbose camel/LLM output. The run manifests
# (data/social_timeline_*.json) already carry per-round timings and counters,
# which is the provenance that matters.
data/overnight_logs/

# Parquet exports are derived artifacts: export_parquet.py regenerates them
# from the .db files in seconds, and the .db files are themselves ignored.
# Committing 6.5 MB of output that is reproducible by one command adds noise
# to every diff and nothing to the record. The exporter and its fidelity gate
# are what need to be under version control, and they are.
data/parquet/

# ---- Simulation output is DERIVED, and git is not where it belongs ----
# `.db` and `data/parquet/` were already excluded on exactly this reasoning.
# Everything below is regenerated from a run's `.db` by analyze.py, dossier.py,
# export_parquet.py, build_package.py or make_timing_charts.py, and together it
# is ~126 MB against 0.4 MB of actual code. The run manifests and analysis JSONs
# are the durable record, so they live in the handover package and the logs --
# not in the history of a fork of someone else's repo.
data/runs/
data/_archive/
data/sim4_package/
data/charts/
data/social_timeline_*.json
data/social_timeline_*.txt
data/sweep18_results.txt
data/load_*.csv
data/night_queue.txt

# Camel/OASIS runtime logs. 163 MB and 1,500 files as of 2026-09-13, one set per
# run (oasis-*, social.agent-*, social.twitter-*, table-*). Derived output, same
# reasoning as the .db and parquet exclusions: nothing in our tooling reads them,
# and every fact a run produces is in its manifest. log/.gitkeep stays tracked so
# the directory still exists on a fresh clone.
log/*.log
data/overnight_cmp_*.txt
data/graph.html

# LLM Bias: oasis.db files are covered by *.db above; decisions/manifests/post banks ARE committed
# (small, and the only record of what each judge chose). Smoke runs are throwaway.
data/llm_bias/runs/smoke*/
data/llm_bias/postbank_s900.jsonl
